# .graphifyignore — what the knowledge graph must NOT index.
# Same syntax as .gitignore. Read `graphify-out/` is TRACKED in this repo, so
# whatever this file lets through ships as the structure map that library
# consumers see first.
#
# PREVENTIVE, NOT CORRECTIVE, AND MEASURED AS SUCH. On 2026-08-22 none of the
# paths below was in the graph: graphify's own defaults already skipped them.
# Proven neutral by running the rebuild twice, with this file and without it --
# both produced 3399 nodes, so it adds nothing and removes nothing. It exists
# because those defaults belong to the tool, not to us: an upgrade can widen
# them, and a graph that quietly starts indexing build output degrades every
# query while still reporting success.
#
# BEFORE ADDING A LINE, KNOW THIS TRAP: `graphify update` REFUSES to write a
# rebuild that has fewer nodes than the current graph, as a guard against a
# broken extraction. Excluding something that IS indexed therefore leaves the
# graph stale WITHOUT an error -- it needs `graphify update --force`. Verify a
# new entry the way this file was verified: rebuild with and without it and
# compare the counts, rather than reasoning about what it ought to match.
#
# THAT REFUSAL IS ALREADY FIRING HERE, FOR REASONS THAT PREDATE THIS FILE.
# The tracked graph carries 3617 nodes; a clean AST re-extraction yields 3399.
# Until that gap is resolved deliberately, every `graphify update` -- including
# the post-commit hook -- declines to write and the tracked graph stays frozen.

# --- Build output -------------------------------------------------------
# Two crates, two target dirs. Derived, enormous, and rebuilt from source.
/target/
/smoke/target/
/smoke/target-matrix/

# --- The graph's own output ---------------------------------------------
# Tracked here (project decision), which means graphify can see it and index
# itself. That is the one growth path the advisory in CLAUDE.md called out.
/graphify-out/

# --- SBTDD process artifacts --------------------------------------------
# Specs, plans and agent config are gitignored and LOCAL to the developer.
# They are also the class the graph is not meant to answer for: questions
# about process go through grep, questions about code go through the graph.
/sbtdd/
/planning/
/plans/
/dev-docs/
/scripts/
/.claude/
/.superpowers/
/.remember/
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/run-tests.py
/claude-usage.txt

# --- VCS and editor ------------------------------------------------------
/.git/
/.idea/
/.vscode/
__pycache__/

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored, so nobody adds them "for tidiness" --------
# src/          the crate
# smoke/src/    the smoke harness — a real consumer of the public API, which
#               is exactly the perspective the graph is least likely to have
# ci/           the invariant checkers are load-bearing logic, not scripts
# tests/        including tests/fixtures/ (42 nodes)
# examples/     the only place some public-API guarantees are proven
# docs/, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, Cargo.toml
#
# ci/fixtures/ is the one open question: 245 nodes (~7% of the graph) of
# redaction self-test fixture data that no code question ever asks about.
# Pruning it would shrink the graph and so needs `update --force`. Left in
# on purpose — that is a decision to take deliberately, not as a side effect
# of adding this file.
